# Placeholder names ONLY — never put real values here, never commit a real .env.
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values there.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKER_URL=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# (MAP_TILE_URL and WORKERS_API_URL were removed 2026-11-18: dead names,
# no code reads them — the map is bundled offline and the Worker URL is
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKER_URL above. Do not re-add them.)
# Sentry error monitoring (free allowance) — WIRED 2026-11-17
# (@sentry/nextjs 10.78.0; apps/web/sentry.{client,server,edge}.config.ts;
# next.config.ts wrapped; tracesSampleRate 0, sendDefaultPii false).
# The founder still creates the DSN in Sentry and pastes it here; never
# commit a real DSN. Until set, Sentry is inactive and errors stay local.
# Exact steps: docs/SENTRY-SETUP.md. Privacy rule: never attach
# coordinates, player names, room codes/IDs, or tokens to Sentry events.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
#
# What each NEXT_PUBLIC_ var is for (public, shipped to the browser):
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL / NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: Supabase
#   project URL + anon/public key (never the service-role key).
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL: canonical site URL, e.g. your *.vercel.app
#   URL. Code default is https://pakdam.example — a placeholder, not a
#   real domain; replace it when the site is deployed.
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKER_URL: deployed Cloudflare Worker base URL, e.g.
#   https://pakdam.<subdomain>.workers.dev. When unset, the web app
#   stays on the local demo loop (see apps/web/src/lib/websocket.ts
#   `isLiveTransportEnabled()`); set it only after `wrangler deploy`
#   succeeds — see docs/DEPLOYMENT-RUNBOOK.md §8.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is a SECRET: Worker secret only
# (`wrangler secret put`), never NEXT_PUBLIC_, never committed.
